# Jira Epic

**Use for:** a milestone, theme, or program of work that will parent multiple
Stories / Bugs / Tasks.

**Create only** when the user explicitly asks for an Epic. Do not invent
epics to satisfy parent-link policy.

## Create

Follow `jira-create` without assigning an epic parent to the Epic itself.
Summary names the theme or milestone outcome.

## Description

```markdown
## Overview

<Why this epic exists, the outcome for the program of work, and boundaries
(in / out of scope) when known.>

## Goals

1. <Theme-level outcome>
2. <...>
```

Do **not** force Story-style Requirements / AC on the Epic. Child issues carry
the measurable 1:1 pairs (`jira-description`). Optional Goals list is enough
for cold readers.

## Children

New Stories, Bugs, and Tasks should link here when this epic is the best fit
(`jira-create` epic parent rules). Do not flood an epic with unrelated chores.

## Done

An Epic is done when its Goals are met and remaining children are Done or
explicitly cut. Status moves: `jira-status`.
